# vendor-patches/services/NiriService.qml.patch
#
# Hyprland action routing for NiriService's socket functions.
#
# Why a patch and not an upstream change: Omarchy's Hyprland speaks the Lua
# dispatcher dialect on its socket (`dispatch X` is shorthand for
# `hl.dispatch(X)`), so the upstream `closewindow address:…` form is a Lua
# syntax error here — verified against the nested compositor (upstream form
# errors, the dsp form replies ok). Upstream inir targets stock Hyprland and
# could never carry dsp-dialect code, so this behavior lives here, applied
# by `scripts/vendor.py --patch` after vendoring. Re-vendoring
# services/NiriService.qml requires re-running `--patch` (it fails loudly
# on drift instead of misapplying silently).
#
# What it changes: when the compositor is Hyprland without Niri,
# closeWindow / focusWindow / moveWindowToWorkspaceById /
# switchToWorkspaceById route through hl.dsp.*, and send() intercepts the
# ToggleWindowFloating action the orbit issues. Every branch falls back to
# the Niri socket path otherwise, so Niri behavior is byte-identical.
# toggleOverview stays Niri-only (its analog is lunana.overview, which has
# no vendor-level handle); float/minimize/restore already have Hyprland
# paths in MinimizedWindows.

--- a/services/NiriService.qml
+++ b/services/NiriService.qml
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 import Quickshell
 import Quickshell.Io
 import Quickshell.Wayland
+import Quickshell.Hyprland
